  "notes": [
    "PR #18 screen content uses production composables; app navigation and IME are covered by native capture scripts.",
    "Each finite destination, permission step, saved/editing/error/busy condition, and recovery input boundary is represented. Animation frames, native credential prompts and physical posture are separate runtime evidence.",
    "Printed-code enrollment, exported draft, readiness, error and busy content use production composables. Permission denial and actual CameraX lifecycle remain native instrumentation coverage; no camera frames enter the catalog.",
    "The channel repair state explains high-priority presentation without a competing notification sound; alarm-volume and heard-sound checks remain separate states. The settings route opens the playback channel, while focus return and persisted channel migration use installed instrumentation.",
    "MainActivity hides a stale recovery state when signed out; account_local represents the resulting signed-out content. Signed-in recovery_empty, recovery_entered and recovery_save fixtures preserve recovery content. These direct composable fixtures do not exercise the activity's signed-out/stale-recovery transition; installed account-navigation acceptance remains missing.",
    "CurfewSettingsScreens routes Sign in (account_local) and Continue setup (account_pending: signed in, unenrolled) to native enrollment; account_enrolled retains Manage account. Existing recovery_empty/recovery_entered/recovery_save fixtures cover the other account branches. The process-recreation AccountSessionPreferences regression covers needsEnrollment state, but screenshot fixtures use empty callbacks and do not prove actual click routing or native account recovery.",
    "These fingerprints record source and fixture review only. Fresh complete screenshot and native CI matrices remain required for this source/coverage version; prior mismatched captures must not be reused. Python coverage-contract checks do not establish rendered appearance, native sign-in, installed behavior or device acceptance.",
    "Bedtime protection is represented by bedtime_access_required, bedtime_ready, bedtime_active and bedtime_interrupted through the production composable with direct state. A protected-work session differs from bedtime_active only in its heading. The navigation rail, landscape navigation bar and top bar are app chrome around these screens and are not screen-content fixtures; their phone, tablet and foldable capture remains outstanding. Route, ViewModel, effect and host files moved out of MainActivity without adding screen states, and their fingerprints record that review only."
  ]
}
